Given an elliptic curve $E$ given by $y^2 = x^3 + Ax + B$:
\begin{enumerate}
	\item Is there are algorithm that decides if $E(\mathbb Z) \setminus\{\infty\}$ is empty?
	\item Is there an algorithm for enumerating $E(\mathbb Z)$?
	\item Can these questions be answered if $E$ is replaced with an arbitrary curve?
\end{enumerate}

Let $X/\mathbb Q$ be a variety, and let $\{Y_a\}_{a\in A}$ be a set of uniformly definable subsets of $X$. 

\begin{enumerate}
\item Is $\overline{Y_a(\mathbb Q)} = Y_a(\mathbb R)$? 
\item Does this imply that $\mathbb Z$ is not diophantine in $\mathbb Q$?
\end{enumerate}
